WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.633
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.903 --> 00:08.530
DEFAMATION LAWSUIT

3
00:08.613 --> 00:11.908
Being sued by such a bigshot politician…

4
00:11.991 --> 00:13.368
It's a special skill.

5
00:13.451 --> 00:14.786
It’s no laughing matter.

6
00:15.954 --> 00:18.456
A claim for 300 million in damages!

7
00:18.540 --> 00:21.042
Guess he's finally out of luck, huh?

8
00:21.125 --> 00:25.296
Knowing that lawyer, he must have some kind of plan.

9
00:25.380 --> 00:27.715
I’m not so sure about this time.

10
00:38.893 --> 00:41.521
Well, let’s see which way the wind blows.

11
00:42.188 --> 00:46.067
The defendant asserted that the plaintiff, Representative Furuse Yoshichika,

12
00:46.150 --> 00:49.612
received slush funds, conducted political maneuvering,

13
00:49.696 --> 00:52.949
and was suspected of involvement in a murder case.

14
00:53.032 --> 00:56.870
They stated as such to RGC Resorts Representative Kang.

15
00:56.953 --> 01:01.416
Do you possess objective evidence to support that assertion?

16
01:02.250 --> 01:03.877
Defense Counsel?

17
01:07.797 --> 01:09.382
We are looking into it.

18
01:09.465 --> 01:12.719
In other words, when you made the assertion to Representative Kang,

19
01:12.802 --> 01:14.512
you did not even have evidence.

20
01:14.596 --> 01:16.264
We are investigating that too.

21
01:16.347 --> 01:17.765
For now, there's no evidence?

22
01:19.851 --> 01:20.894
Go ahead.

23
01:22.520 --> 01:27.025
This is the file the defendant presented to Representative Kang.

24
01:27.108 --> 01:30.737
It contains serious accusations, claiming money was used as slush funds

25
01:30.820 --> 01:33.364
and that Furuse ordered articles fabricated

26
01:33.865 --> 01:36.659
for use in political strategies.

27
01:36.743 --> 01:38.703
Yet, according to the defendant,

28
01:40.038 --> 01:42.916
there is not a single piece of evidence.

29
01:43.666 --> 01:47.128
Furthermore, this magazine was never even published.

30
01:47.211 --> 01:48.588
Defense Counsel,

31
01:48.671 --> 01:53.843
can you present objective evidence to support your claims?

32
02:00.266 --> 02:01.351
We're looking into it.

33
02:01.935 --> 02:04.103
Defense Counsel,

34
02:04.187 --> 02:07.106
please review and secure evidence before the next session.

35
02:07.190 --> 02:09.400
NO EVIDENCE

36
02:09.484 --> 02:11.194
ORDERED A TABLOID TO FABRICATE ARTICLES?

37
02:12.862 --> 02:16.032
If we don't have some kind of evidence, we’re going to lose!

38
02:16.115 --> 02:18.284
-Evidence of wrongdoing? -Yes!

39
02:18.368 --> 02:21.496
Anything connecting Furuse and Sendo.

40
02:21.579 --> 02:25.667
You say that, but Sendo is taking all the blame.

41
02:25.750 --> 02:28.962
The money trail might not lead back to Furuse.

42
02:29.045 --> 02:31.214
What about witnesses or a whistleblower?

43
02:31.297 --> 02:34.384
Trying to find someone now is going to be tough.

44
02:34.467 --> 02:35.885
It doesn't matter.

45
02:36.761 --> 02:40.014
I don't care whether we win or lose the trial.

46
02:40.598 --> 02:43.101
No, we're talking about 300 million here!

47
02:43.184 --> 02:45.645
The 300 million is just a threat.

48
02:48.481 --> 02:51.401
If they sue for obstruction of business and defamation,

49
02:51.484 --> 02:53.277
it will be ten million at most.

50
02:53.361 --> 02:57.281
Even ten million is a bit tough for us, though.

51
02:57.365 --> 03:00.535
This trial has only one purpose.

52
03:01.160 --> 03:06.207
To drag them into court.

53
03:07.625 --> 03:09.752
We received a report from Mr. Shoji.

54
03:09.836 --> 03:12.839
The Uramawashi side has no means of proving anything.

55
03:12.922 --> 03:15.091
Hmm? Of course.

56
03:15.174 --> 03:17.719
We’re not doing anything illegal, after all.

57
03:17.802 --> 03:19.679
Looks like a guaranteed win.

58
03:20.304 --> 03:21.514
More importantly,

59
03:21.597 --> 03:25.727
we caused quite a bit of trouble for Representative Kang, didn't we?

60
03:25.810 --> 03:28.438
I will apologize to him once more.

61
03:29.022 --> 03:30.815
All that’s left is the trial.

62
03:31.816 --> 03:33.443
Win or lose,

63
03:33.526 --> 03:37.822
they can't keep interfering with our resort project.

64
03:40.783 --> 03:42.076
That said,

65
03:42.702 --> 03:44.996
the wind is blowing in our favor.

66
04:18.654 --> 04:20.782
I heard from Mr. Kureta.

67
04:20.865 --> 04:23.076
He said you covered for them.

68
04:26.120 --> 04:29.665
Could it be you are starting to have doubts about Mr. Furuse?

69
04:29.749 --> 04:30.917
That was

70
04:32.377 --> 04:33.920
just a passing whim.

71
04:39.175 --> 04:43.846
Mr. Furuse is like a father to me.

72
04:43.930 --> 04:44.931
Besides,

73
04:45.765 --> 04:49.602
I cannot trust that Uramawashi man.

74
04:53.898 --> 04:55.233
Donghyuk,

75
04:56.275 --> 04:58.403
don't you want to know the truth?

76
05:00.113 --> 05:02.657
When you hide something or lie to yourself,

77
05:02.740 --> 05:05.159
tragedy is always born from lies.

78
05:08.579 --> 05:12.125
I simply want to bring the truth to light.

79
05:14.710 --> 05:15.878
Hey.

80
05:15.962 --> 05:17.046
What?

81
05:17.130 --> 05:19.340
-Can he really be trusted? -Who knows…

82
05:19.424 --> 05:20.842
But, last time…

83
05:22.844 --> 05:24.303
Annyeonghaseyo.

84
05:24.387 --> 05:25.680
Hello.

85
05:27.432 --> 05:28.641
Yo.

86
05:29.267 --> 05:31.436
You finally came to see me, huh?

87
05:32.311 --> 05:35.022
I still don't trust you.

88
05:35.565 --> 05:41.195
I only came to help Yukari bring the truth to light.

89
05:41.279 --> 05:43.739
A formidable rival, I see.

90
05:45.783 --> 05:49.245
So, what is it that you want to know?

91
05:50.288 --> 05:54.292
You used Yukari to get me to come here.

92
05:54.375 --> 05:58.045
There must be something you want to know, right?

93
05:58.129 --> 05:59.130
Exactly.

94
06:00.256 --> 06:04.969
Capable men always get straight to the point. I like that.

95
06:06.387 --> 06:07.263
Transcripts?

96
06:07.346 --> 06:08.181
Yes.

97
06:08.264 --> 06:13.728
Transcripts of the meetings between the RGC side and Japan's resort project team.

98
06:15.855 --> 06:17.398
Everything from recent years--

99
06:17.481 --> 06:19.233
Wait a minute.

100
06:19.317 --> 06:21.360
If he gives us the transcripts, he will--

101
06:21.444 --> 06:23.487
We won't submit them as evidence.

102
06:25.156 --> 06:27.533
We’ll merely use them for reference.

103
06:27.617 --> 06:29.410
-But-- -I…

104
06:30.244 --> 06:36.209
"I played by the rules and gave it my all. I have no regrets."

105
06:37.210 --> 06:41.589
When you fail to save Miyuki, can you say that?

106
06:42.632 --> 06:44.008
I don't mind.

107
06:47.511 --> 06:50.640
I will show you the transcripts.

108
06:53.100 --> 06:56.270
I also only wish for one thing.

109
06:58.147 --> 07:00.024
I want to know the truth.

110
07:03.986 --> 07:05.112
RESORT PROJECT TRANSCRIPTS

111
07:05.196 --> 07:07.698
They are all uploaded here.

112
07:08.241 --> 07:11.118
Regular meetings, company selection meetings,

113
07:11.202 --> 07:14.330
financial reporting meetings, meetings this, meetings that…

114
07:14.413 --> 07:17.208
It’s a national project, it's only natural to have so many…

115
07:17.291 --> 07:18.167
Excuse me.

116
07:20.753 --> 07:23.506
How many pages is this for just one meeting?

117
07:23.589 --> 07:27.176
-Are we going to read all of this? -First, go back five years.

118
07:27.802 --> 07:32.515
Write down every single company name that appears in the transcripts.

119
07:32.598 --> 07:34.308
-Five years? -All of them?

120
07:34.392 --> 07:36.227
All right, let's do this!

121
07:36.310 --> 07:38.521
Compared to the bar exam, this is nothing!

122
07:39.146 --> 07:40.481
Here you go.

123
07:40.565 --> 07:43.651
Let's do our best. Right? Ms. Aso. Let's work together.

124
07:43.734 --> 07:44.610
COPYING DATA

125
07:45.486 --> 07:47.572
Mitsukura &amp; Co…

126
07:47.655 --> 07:48.698
Habu!

127
07:49.323 --> 07:51.826
Wouldn't it be easier to use AI for this? Look.

128
07:51.909 --> 07:53.786
Nakazaki, you're so smart sometimes!

129
07:53.869 --> 07:56.289
Here, the name is cut off midway.

130
07:56.372 --> 07:59.834
This translation app is no good. It's strangely off.

131
08:00.376 --> 08:02.670
You're right, it abbreviated a lot.

132
08:02.753 --> 08:04.297
Nichio Construction.

133
08:04.380 --> 08:08.301
-Kagura Urban Development. -Toto Electric.

134
08:08.384 --> 08:10.344
Yasui Securities.

135
08:10.428 --> 08:12.138
T&amp;U Agency. Mitsukura &amp; Co.

136
08:12.221 --> 08:14.348
I already added Mitsukura &amp; Co.

137
08:14.432 --> 08:17.435
Bring the companies that came up more than once over here.

138
08:17.518 --> 08:18.728
Keiyo Travel--

139
08:19.729 --> 08:21.272
I bought some food!

140
08:22.315 --> 08:25.151
Nakazaki, you're amazing! It's all about the salmon!

141
08:25.234 --> 08:27.236
-Right? -You're drinking again.

142
08:27.320 --> 08:29.530
At this hour, drinking makes me work faster.

143
08:29.614 --> 08:30.656
Is that really true?

144
08:30.740 --> 08:32.825
Okay. Let's work even harder!

145
08:34.493 --> 08:36.787
-Do we have tuna or kombu? -No.

146
08:41.167 --> 08:43.210
What a big network!

147
08:43.294 --> 08:45.296
As expected, it’s all big corporations.

148
08:45.379 --> 08:47.715
Well, it’s a national project.

149
08:50.426 --> 08:52.136
Done! Five years' worth.

150
09:00.519 --> 09:02.521
CONSTRUCTION / ENERGY

151
09:03.939 --> 09:05.650
-Wait! -Hey!

152
09:05.733 --> 09:07.943
-Hold on a second! -Why are you doing that?

153
09:08.027 --> 09:10.029
We put in so much effort!

154
09:10.112 --> 09:11.906
Oh no, wait a minute!

155
09:11.989 --> 09:14.325
-The fruits of our all-nighter! -Why?

156
09:23.542 --> 09:25.544
The companies left here…

157
09:26.045 --> 09:28.673
Investigate them again, in detail.

158
09:29.298 --> 09:30.257
Huh?

159
09:31.050 --> 09:34.804
But aren't these all companies we've never heard of before?

160
09:34.887 --> 09:36.555
That’s precisely why.

161
09:37.932 --> 09:40.726
They are companies that normally shouldn't be involved

162
09:40.810 --> 09:41.894
in a national project.

163
09:41.977 --> 09:44.939
Why are they here? Here!

164
09:45.022 --> 09:49.026
You mean, they may be pawns for someone in power.

165
09:49.110 --> 09:51.737
Correct. You've gotten better at this.

166
09:51.821 --> 09:52.988
I see.

167
09:53.072 --> 09:55.866
All right, let's look into these companies.

168
09:55.950 --> 09:59.912
President, board members, business details, everything.

169
09:59.995 --> 10:01.664
-Yes. -Okay.

170
10:01.747 --> 10:06.293
The Uramawashi side has not submitted any new briefs or evidence.

171
10:06.961 --> 10:09.505
If they cannot submit anything by the next hearing,

172
10:09.588 --> 10:13.092
the court will decide that there is no need to continue any further

173
10:13.175 --> 10:15.302
and will close the case.

174
10:16.178 --> 10:19.557
They say a cornered rat will bite the cat.

175
10:21.058 --> 10:23.352
T&amp;U Agency?

176
10:24.103 --> 10:25.354
Yes.

177
10:25.438 --> 10:29.191
A small advertising agency with only 15 employees.

178
10:29.275 --> 10:33.112
Normally, a company this small wouldn't be in a national project, right?

179
10:33.195 --> 10:36.490
They are developing the payment system to be used in the resort.

180
10:36.574 --> 10:37.491
Payment system?

181
10:37.575 --> 10:39.076
An ad agency?

182
10:40.911 --> 10:42.788
I remember this company.

183
10:43.414 --> 10:44.457
Really?

184
10:44.540 --> 10:45.374
Yes.

185
10:45.458 --> 10:48.294
RGC said this company had no track record,

186
10:48.377 --> 10:51.756
so it would be difficult to let them work on the project,

187
10:52.298 --> 10:53.591
but the Japanese insisted.

188
10:53.674 --> 10:55.176
The Japanese…

189
10:55.676 --> 10:58.262
So a politician?

190
10:58.345 --> 10:59.638
Yes.

191
10:59.722 --> 11:02.308
I remember Mr. Furuse intervening in its favor.

192
11:02.391 --> 11:04.935
It's really fishy, isn't it?

193
11:06.937 --> 11:09.148
There’s one more thing.

194
11:11.776 --> 11:15.946
Among the board members, there is an interesting man.

195
11:21.869 --> 11:26.540
As before, the defendant has submitted no objective evidence proving

196
11:26.624 --> 11:28.042
the plaintiff's wrongdoing.

197
11:28.125 --> 11:30.461
-Therefore-- -Your Honor.

198
11:31.170 --> 11:33.172
I'm submitting

199
11:35.424 --> 11:36.800
new evidence.

200
11:38.594 --> 11:43.766
T&amp;U Agency, an advertising agency with 15 employees.

201
11:44.391 --> 11:46.852
The director, Kazuhiko Kiriyama,

202
11:46.936 --> 11:50.523
is the son of Kotaro Kiriyama, head of Mr. Furuse's supporters' association.

203
11:51.357 --> 11:53.817
He produced election posters for Mr. Furuse for years,

204
11:53.901 --> 11:55.694
as well as his newsletter and website--

205
11:55.778 --> 11:58.364
This is a defamation lawsuit.

206
11:59.573 --> 12:02.535
Who produces the election posters is not relevant.

207
12:02.618 --> 12:03.953
The defendant’s conclusion--

208
12:04.537 --> 12:11.126
What was this company tasked to do in this resort project?

209
12:12.795 --> 12:14.838
System development.

210
12:16.757 --> 12:18.759
Worth 2.7 billion yen.

211
12:19.552 --> 12:22.304
This system is already undergoing trial operation

212
12:22.388 --> 12:25.266
and is scheduled to be introduced at the next Expo.

213
12:25.349 --> 12:28.143
They seem to be quite trusted.

214
12:28.227 --> 12:32.648
However, T&amp;U Agency has no track record in system development.

215
12:32.731 --> 12:35.526
The actual development has been outsourced.

216
12:36.235 --> 12:39.405
And this payment system has a catch.

217
12:41.156 --> 12:42.366
A PROFIT-GENERATING LOOP

218
12:42.449 --> 12:47.496
At the resort, certain products and services will have reduced tax.

219
12:47.580 --> 12:51.083
The reduced amount is added to the payment system's transaction fees.

220
12:51.166 --> 12:52.251
In other words,

221
12:52.334 --> 12:54.628
a company with no track record,

222
12:54.712 --> 12:58.757
which has supported Mr. Furuse's political activities for many years,

223
12:58.841 --> 13:01.260
now has exclusive access

224
13:02.011 --> 13:06.223
to a business that continues to generate vast profits.

225
13:06.307 --> 13:07.349
Your Honor!

226
13:07.433 --> 13:09.810
This evidence doesn't prove the plaintiff profits from this!

227
13:09.893 --> 13:11.812
-This is unfair! -Well then…

228
13:14.106 --> 13:16.066
Let's ask him in person.

229
13:18.193 --> 13:24.408
The defense calls for an examination of the plaintiff,

230
13:25.326 --> 13:28.162
Mr. Furuse Yoshichika.

231
13:30.581 --> 13:32.791
The tide of the trial has changed.

232
13:32.875 --> 13:35.586
I think even Furuse's side is flustered.

233
13:35.669 --> 13:37.463
If we break them down here,

234
13:37.546 --> 13:40.924
I think there will also be progress in Mr. Takeshi Nitou's case.

235
13:41.759 --> 13:43.761
Is that what my brother said?

236
13:44.928 --> 13:47.890
Not in those exact words,

237
13:47.973 --> 13:50.476
but I'm sure he has something in mind.

238
13:52.311 --> 13:54.021
Please be very careful.

239
13:54.521 --> 13:59.151
Back then, they produced evidence and testimony out of nowhere,

240
13:59.234 --> 14:01.570
and in an instant, the tide turned.

241
14:03.989 --> 14:05.157
It’s all right.

242
14:05.658 --> 14:09.828
I promise I will win this trial, and the retrial too.

243
14:10.788 --> 14:12.498
Let's hang in there together.

244
14:13.207 --> 14:14.667
For Taiji's sake too.

245
14:16.001 --> 14:17.127
Yeah.

246
14:17.211 --> 14:18.837
Moving on to the next news.

247
14:18.921 --> 14:24.093
The lawsuit between Mr. Furuse and Attorney Naotoshi Uramawashi

248
14:24.176 --> 14:25.844
has had a new development.

249
14:25.928 --> 14:29.932
The defense side has applied to examine Mr. Furuse himself.

250
14:30.474 --> 14:32.309
-The plaintiff side… -Mr. Furuse…

251
14:32.393 --> 14:34.144
I wonder if he'll come.

252
14:34.812 --> 14:36.355
I don't know.

253
14:37.356 --> 14:38.816
But it’s our chance.

254
14:39.400 --> 14:42.569
Donghyuk, I have one more request.

255
14:44.279 --> 14:48.325
Could you testify as a witness for the defense side?

256
14:49.368 --> 14:50.661
That is--

257
14:50.744 --> 14:52.037
I know.

258
14:52.121 --> 14:53.789
If you take the witness stand,

259
14:53.872 --> 14:56.834
you will be in complete opposition to Mr. Furuse.

260
14:58.293 --> 15:01.839
But, I want to resolve the case here.

261
15:08.012 --> 15:09.138
Very well.

262
15:09.638 --> 15:11.265
Thank you very much.

263
15:13.142 --> 15:16.895
I also have something I want to speak to you about.

264
15:16.979 --> 15:18.188
What?

265
15:35.289 --> 15:36.707
Thank you.

266
16:13.994 --> 16:17.581
This is the last piece.

267
16:24.671 --> 16:30.677
Only after doubting everything does the truth become visible.

268
16:32.930 --> 16:34.681
What is the meaning of this?

269
16:34.765 --> 16:35.891
I am terribly sorry.

270
16:35.974 --> 16:38.602
-I didn't think they could-- -Enough with the excuses.

271
16:39.228 --> 16:42.648
Please tell me what we are going to do from here.

272
16:46.485 --> 16:49.363
You came here because you have a plan, right?

273
16:50.405 --> 16:52.282
No, about that…

274
16:56.620 --> 16:57.788
Murota,

275
16:58.956 --> 17:00.207
what do you think?

276
17:10.801 --> 17:11.927
Excuse me.

277
17:13.137 --> 17:14.638
We were waiting for you.

278
17:20.853 --> 17:21.854
FOURTH HEARING

279
17:21.937 --> 17:24.648
We understand Mr. Furuse is to be examined today,

280
17:24.731 --> 17:29.444
but it seems he has official duties today and won't be able to attend.

281
17:30.320 --> 17:33.949
We will move Mr. Furuse's examination to a later time.

282
17:34.032 --> 17:36.702
Now, let's proceed with the witness examination,

283
17:36.785 --> 17:38.745
originally scheduled after that.

284
17:40.080 --> 17:42.749
Witness for the defense, Lee Donghyuk.

285
17:44.334 --> 17:46.003
DEFENSE WITNESS EXAMINATION

286
17:46.086 --> 17:49.715
Having T&amp;U Agency participate in the resort project

287
17:49.798 --> 17:51.258
was Mr. Furuse's call, right?

288
17:52.593 --> 17:53.719
That is incorrect.

289
17:54.303 --> 17:57.264
Mr. Furuse was not involved at all.

290
18:00.559 --> 18:01.894
Please wait.

291
18:01.977 --> 18:04.605
As the negotiator for the RGC side,

292
18:04.688 --> 18:06.982
you had many discussions with Mr. Furuse, correct?

293
18:07.065 --> 18:09.568
I only had discussions with Mr. Murota.

294
18:10.277 --> 18:14.198
Were you ever requested by Mr. Furuse to use T&amp;U?

295
18:14.281 --> 18:15.115
No.

296
18:15.199 --> 18:18.160
The one who gave the instructions was Mr. Furuse, right?

297
18:18.243 --> 18:19.286
It was Mr. Murota.

298
18:20.412 --> 18:21.538
Really?

299
18:22.122 --> 18:23.290
Yes.

300
18:26.001 --> 18:29.171
Defense Counsel, will that be all?

301
18:29.713 --> 18:30.547
Yes.

302
18:33.175 --> 18:35.594
We will now conclude the witness examination

303
18:35.677 --> 18:37.721
of Mr. Lee Donghyuk.

304
18:41.391 --> 18:45.395
Next, witness for the plaintiff, Takashi Murota.

305
18:46.021 --> 18:48.148
PLAINTIFF WITNESS EXAMINATION

306
18:48.232 --> 18:49.233
Witness,

307
18:49.942 --> 18:54.279
regarding T&amp;U Agency's participation in the resort project,

308
18:54.363 --> 18:57.991
did you ever receive instructions from Mr. Furuse?

309
18:58.742 --> 18:59.743
No.

310
19:00.661 --> 19:01.787
Then,

311
19:03.747 --> 19:06.208
who made the decision?

312
19:08.252 --> 19:09.378
It was me.

313
19:10.587 --> 19:12.047
T&amp;U's participation

314
19:12.130 --> 19:15.884
and the contract for the payment system were all my decisions.

315
19:15.968 --> 19:17.803
It’s a 2.7 billion yen contract!

316
19:17.886 --> 19:20.430
A secretary can't do it without Mr. Furuse's--

317
19:20.514 --> 19:22.516
Mr. Furuse does not know.

318
19:22.599 --> 19:24.810
He was never involved in this matter.

319
19:26.019 --> 19:29.564
All responsibility lies with me.

320
19:35.195 --> 19:37.489
A scapegoat.

321
19:38.865 --> 19:39.992
I see.

322
19:40.701 --> 19:42.327
ACTED BEHIND HIS BACK?

323
19:45.372 --> 19:46.832
Good work.

324
19:46.915 --> 19:49.418
I’m glad to have been of service.

325
19:49.501 --> 19:51.628
The opponent must not have expected it.

326
19:51.712 --> 19:55.465
With this, the hand of the law can't touch you now.

327
19:56.216 --> 20:00.053
Murota, I'm sorry, for making you take the fall.

328
20:00.137 --> 20:01.138
Yes.

329
20:04.641 --> 20:07.644
It will be all right, won't it, Mr. Shoji?

330
20:07.728 --> 20:09.021
Oh, yes.

331
20:09.104 --> 20:11.940
If they cannot prove that Mr. Murota received money,

332
20:12.024 --> 20:13.233
he will not be indicted.

333
20:13.317 --> 20:14.609
Please rest assured.

334
20:14.693 --> 20:16.570
Will it really be all right?

335
20:20.157 --> 20:21.908
What’s wrong?

336
20:22.743 --> 20:25.704
If you want to be my successor, you can't show weakness.

337
20:26.330 --> 20:28.373
Keep your mind strong.

338
20:28.457 --> 20:29.416
Yes.

339
20:31.752 --> 20:33.211
It will be fine.

340
20:34.713 --> 20:37.257
I always tie up loose ends.

341
20:37.341 --> 20:43.597
No matter what happens, I will take care of you and your family,

342
20:43.680 --> 20:45.265
-Don't worry. -Yes.

343
21:04.743 --> 21:07.704
-Yes? -Mr. Takashi Murota?

344
21:07.788 --> 21:09.373
I'm Matoba from the MPD.

345
21:09.998 --> 21:13.627
May we discuss the resort project?

346
21:16.171 --> 21:17.214
Sure.

347
21:26.181 --> 21:27.516
Where are we?

348
21:27.599 --> 21:30.977
The media is camped out front. We’ll enter through the back.

349
21:33.605 --> 21:36.775
Mr. Furuse already spoke to you, right? Let's settle this quietly…

350
21:40.987 --> 21:42.823
About the payment system,

351
21:42.906 --> 21:45.826
was it really a decision you made on your own?

352
21:45.909 --> 21:46.827
Yes.

353
21:47.702 --> 21:53.792
I caused Mr. Furuse worry and trouble in a matter he had no knowledge of.

354
21:54.418 --> 21:55.544
I see.

355
21:56.044 --> 22:00.507
The reason we had you come here today is actually for a different matter.

356
22:04.469 --> 22:08.223
The murder of Takeshi Nitou, by Miyuki Shiramoto.

357
22:08.306 --> 22:10.392
There has been new information.

358
22:12.394 --> 22:15.147
Actually, a certain item was found.

359
22:15.730 --> 22:16.648
What?

360
22:22.612 --> 22:23.780
Yes?

361
22:23.864 --> 22:25.448
Mr. Furuse.

362
22:25.532 --> 22:26.700
What is it?

363
22:26.783 --> 22:28.577
We have a problem.

364
23:07.407 --> 23:08.491
Donghyuk?

365
23:10.994 --> 23:12.162
Donghyuk?

366
23:12.913 --> 23:15.749
It was like this, wasn't it?

367
23:18.376 --> 23:21.004
Back then, this was a multi-story parking lot.

368
23:21.755 --> 23:24.049
No one remembers anymore, though.

369
23:24.132 --> 23:28.428
And, the incident that happened…

370
23:29.721 --> 23:32.474
There are hardly any people left who remember it.

371
23:34.309 --> 23:35.894
What are you talking about?

372
23:43.944 --> 23:45.320
Murota?

373
23:47.072 --> 23:49.950
Those are real investigators.

374
23:51.451 --> 23:53.870
He would never doubt them.

375
23:54.621 --> 23:57.290
We found Takeshi Nitou's suicide note.

376
24:00.126 --> 24:03.380
Just a short while ago, Mr. Furuse submitted it.

377
24:03.463 --> 24:04.714
He did?

378
24:06.216 --> 24:08.134
He said he found it in your desk.

379
24:08.218 --> 24:09.594
What?

380
24:11.888 --> 24:16.601
The one who set it all up was you, wasn't it?

381
24:19.437 --> 24:21.564
He's setting me up for this too…

382
24:21.648 --> 24:23.984
This is a childish trick.

383
24:26.027 --> 24:28.154
I didn't want to do it! But he…

384
24:29.239 --> 24:30.448
What's wrong?

385
24:31.157 --> 24:32.701
What about him?

386
24:33.910 --> 24:35.161
Tell us everything.

387
24:37.497 --> 24:39.165
Do you understand now?

388
24:40.083 --> 24:43.086
Furuse is not going to protect you.

389
24:47.549 --> 24:50.552
I didn't have a choice!

390
24:52.804 --> 24:54.180
You're playing dirty.

391
24:54.264 --> 24:55.640
You too.

392
24:55.724 --> 24:58.059
You guys are the same, right?

393
24:58.810 --> 25:04.607
Well, no matter what he says, it has nothing to do with me.

394
25:04.691 --> 25:06.693
You're being quite cold.

395
25:07.527 --> 25:09.696
He's your successor, isn't he?

396
25:10.280 --> 25:11.906
Successor?

397
25:15.410 --> 25:20.707
This line of work isn't for the faint of heart.

398
25:21.916 --> 25:26.671
Besides, I can easily find a replacement secretary.

399
25:29.174 --> 25:30.216
Did you hear that?

400
25:40.643 --> 25:42.395
We never said the video was live.

401
25:42.479 --> 25:44.439
You were completely fooled.

402
25:44.939 --> 25:46.983
Hurry!

403
25:49.611 --> 25:51.404
Oh no!

404
25:58.578 --> 26:00.497
You understand now, don't you?

405
26:01.081 --> 26:05.835
Furuse does not plan to protect you.

406
26:07.379 --> 26:11.132
I'm a busy man, so if you'll excuse me.

407
26:11.716 --> 26:17.222
No turning back now. Why not see it through?

408
26:18.807 --> 26:20.100
The players are all here.

409
26:22.644 --> 26:24.187
You have the best seat.

410
26:25.230 --> 26:27.857
Now, can you tell us the truth?

411
26:32.821 --> 26:34.280
During land development--

412
26:34.364 --> 26:35.198
Murota.

413
26:43.498 --> 26:48.086
During the land development, people complained of a foul odor.

414
26:48.586 --> 26:51.423
We oppose the redevelopment!

415
26:51.506 --> 26:54.175
We oppose the redevelopment!

416
26:54.259 --> 26:57.887
The opposition was fierce, so we tested the water immediately.

417
26:57.971 --> 27:01.808
Just before the results came out, Mr. Furuse called me in.

418
27:01.891 --> 27:04.894
Mr. Nitou is an upright man.

419
27:05.478 --> 27:06.980
I'm counting on you.

420
27:07.063 --> 27:08.314
Very well.

421
27:08.898 --> 27:12.402
Back then, I was his second secretary.

422
27:13.194 --> 27:14.654
He told me to fake the data.

423
27:14.737 --> 27:16.573
LOWEST VALUES

424
27:18.575 --> 27:21.744
However, Ms. Shiramoto doubted the test results,

425
27:21.828 --> 27:23.455
investigated independently,

426
27:23.538 --> 27:26.291
and found out that the numbers didn't add up.

427
27:26.875 --> 27:30.462
Receiving that report, Mr. Nitou realized the falsification…

428
27:31.754 --> 27:34.048
Do you understand what you've done?

429
27:34.966 --> 27:39.429
But these documents are submitted under your name. It's already too late--

430
27:39.512 --> 27:40.889
You bastard!

431
27:40.972 --> 27:43.516
What's wrong? You're being so loud.

432
27:43.600 --> 27:44.601
Oh, no…

433
27:48.021 --> 27:49.105
Mr. Nitou,

434
27:49.856 --> 27:53.318
I highly value your honesty.

435
27:54.444 --> 27:58.239
However, politics isn't so straightforward.

436
27:58.323 --> 28:01.576
I would like you to be a bit more understanding.

437
28:01.659 --> 28:03.077
But this is falsification.

438
28:03.161 --> 28:05.246
Only if someone finds out.

439
28:07.582 --> 28:08.625
Listen carefully.

440
28:10.210 --> 28:12.295
If this problem comes to light,

441
28:12.378 --> 28:15.381
the one held accountable will be you, Mr. Nitou.

442
28:17.175 --> 28:21.221
Of course, it could also become a problem for me and the entire party.

443
28:21.888 --> 28:23.431
That's not all.

444
28:24.807 --> 28:28.269
The tens of thousands of people involved in this plan,

445
28:28.353 --> 28:31.272
and the lives of their families,

446
28:33.650 --> 28:35.235
will be greatly affected.

447
28:37.654 --> 28:43.910
Are you prepared to sacrifice all that just to stick to your honesty?

448
28:45.995 --> 28:48.039
Do you have that resolve?

449
28:52.085 --> 28:53.795
Do you, Mr. Nitou?

450
29:02.512 --> 29:03.680
My apologies.

451
29:08.142 --> 29:09.561
However…

452
29:10.603 --> 29:12.730
You don't need to worry.

453
29:13.398 --> 29:15.733
I always tie up loose ends.

454
29:17.318 --> 29:18.736
No matter what happens,

455
29:19.904 --> 29:23.241
I will take good care of you

456
29:24.117 --> 29:26.828
and your family, Mr. Nitou.

457
29:27.954 --> 29:29.080
Got it?

458
29:33.293 --> 29:37.297
Mr. Furuse asked me to keep an eye on Mr. Nitou.

459
29:46.389 --> 29:47.807
And…

460
29:48.808 --> 29:50.935
I lost sight of him for a brief moment…

461
30:00.278 --> 30:03.990
I tried to call out to him, but it happened in a split second.

462
30:08.536 --> 30:09.746
What?

463
30:29.223 --> 30:30.433
Mr. Nitou!

464
30:35.855 --> 30:37.065
Suicide?

465
30:42.153 --> 30:45.823
Mr. Furuse hated being investigated.

466
30:45.907 --> 30:47.116
It was then that…

467
30:48.952 --> 30:50.536
Oh, please wait a moment.

468
30:57.585 --> 30:59.921
MIYUKI SHIRAMOTO ABOUT THE WATER POLLUTION

469
31:00.964 --> 31:02.048
Sir.

470
31:02.966 --> 31:04.509
I have an idea.

471
31:05.718 --> 31:06.552
Yes.

472
31:07.261 --> 31:08.346
Yes.

473
31:09.013 --> 31:14.227
I used Mr. Nitou's phone to send a message to Ms. Shiramoto and called her over.

474
31:23.444 --> 31:25.154
Mr. Nitou.

475
31:40.545 --> 31:43.256
Mr. Nitou!

476
31:46.175 --> 31:48.803
Mr. Nitou, can you hear me?

477
31:49.303 --> 31:53.516
After that, you pulled the strings.

478
31:55.685 --> 31:57.103
Right?

479
31:57.186 --> 31:58.563
JUSTICE'S FORM WAS A SHAM

480
31:59.313 --> 32:00.648
SHE'S A HYPOCRITE MURDERER!

481
32:00.732 --> 32:04.569
A righteous lawyer was actually involved in shady deals

482
32:04.652 --> 32:06.487
and eventually committed murder.

483
32:06.571 --> 32:07.739
That was the story.

484
32:09.073 --> 32:11.117
The public took the bait.

485
32:11.200 --> 32:13.453
IT'S UNTHINKABLE THAT A DEFENDER OF THE PEOPLE WOULD DO THIS

486
32:13.536 --> 32:16.539
No, not just the public!

487
32:16.622 --> 32:17.707
At that time,

488
32:17.790 --> 32:22.003
even though there was a discrepancy in Mr. Nitou's estimated time of death,

489
32:22.086 --> 32:24.756
no one inside the police force pointed it out.

490
32:26.132 --> 32:30.261
Thus, Ms. Shiramoto was framed for a crime she didn't commit.

491
32:33.222 --> 32:34.557
I always…

492
32:37.810 --> 32:40.146
I always found it strange.

493
32:40.646 --> 32:44.692
I also have something I want to speak to you about.

494
32:45.401 --> 32:46.402
What?

495
32:47.236 --> 32:49.447
I received a message from my father.

496
32:50.073 --> 32:52.075
The day before he died.

497
32:52.825 --> 32:54.327
From your father?

498
32:54.410 --> 32:55.328
Yes.

499
32:55.411 --> 32:58.289
BE STRONG. I'M PROUD OF YOU.

500
33:01.250 --> 33:04.295
Back then, we were living far apart,

501
33:04.378 --> 33:07.256
so I thought he only sent it to cheer me on.

502
33:08.341 --> 33:10.802
-But thinking about it now-- -This was…

503
33:12.470 --> 33:13.638
A will.

504
33:16.641 --> 33:21.104
There was no way they could find the true culprit.

505
33:22.855 --> 33:24.982
Because it was suicide, after all.

506
33:27.151 --> 33:29.153
In order to find out the truth,

507
33:29.237 --> 33:33.950
we needed you and Murota to fight us in court.

508
33:34.033 --> 33:39.080
That's why… I provoked you into filing the lawsuit.

509
33:39.163 --> 33:44.794
Donghyuk intentionally let you know he would stand as a witness for the defense.

510
33:44.877 --> 33:49.507
Seeing that things were going sour, you used this chance to cut Murota loose.

511
33:50.341 --> 33:55.138
From the moment we framed Tajima and returned Murota to your side,

512
33:55.221 --> 33:57.515
this operation had already begun.

513
33:58.015 --> 33:59.642
-Murota. -Yes.

514
33:59.725 --> 34:02.353
I'll need you to come back here soon.

515
34:02.436 --> 34:03.855
I understand.

516
34:04.564 --> 34:07.525
You thought you had us in the palm of your hand,

517
34:08.651 --> 34:12.488
but you were the one being played.

518
34:17.535 --> 34:18.744
So what?

519
34:19.453 --> 34:21.289
You are lawyers, aren't you?

520
34:21.956 --> 34:26.169
You should proceed based on facts, not wild assertions.

521
34:27.044 --> 34:30.423
Do you have any evidence for what you just said?

522
34:30.506 --> 34:31.507
Well?

523
34:35.636 --> 34:37.430
We found a suicide note.

524
34:39.348 --> 34:42.852
You really never learn, do you? That nonsense again…

525
34:42.935 --> 34:45.229
How do you know it's nonsense?

526
34:48.566 --> 34:50.318
Sir, I'm sorry.

527
34:53.946 --> 34:56.115
"I'm sorry" isn't going to cut it.

528
34:56.199 --> 34:59.243
Back then, you never mentioned this.

529
35:01.078 --> 35:02.914
Is this another one of your lies?

530
35:02.997 --> 35:05.082
Well? Is it?

531
35:05.708 --> 35:07.376
"Back then"…

532
35:08.169 --> 35:10.379
When are you referring to?

533
35:13.716 --> 35:17.595
This is the record of the data falsification that Mr. Murota carried out.

534
35:21.265 --> 35:22.850
In any case,

535
35:23.851 --> 35:25.686
it has nothing to do with me.

536
35:25.770 --> 35:27.730
You don't get it, do you?

537
35:28.231 --> 35:30.441
Because you ran your mouth,

538
35:30.942 --> 35:34.195
Murota's testimony turned into certainty.

539
35:34.779 --> 35:37.907
On top of that, if we have the falsified data,

540
35:37.990 --> 35:43.037
we can prove without a doubt Mr. Takeshi Nitou's suicide as well.

541
35:44.789 --> 35:46.123
Ridiculous.

542
35:51.295 --> 35:55.424
Not a bad story, Mr. Uramawashi.

543
35:57.635 --> 35:59.136
As fiction, that is.

544
35:59.637 --> 36:01.555
It's non-fiction, though.

545
36:04.934 --> 36:05.935
Wait!

546
36:10.189 --> 36:11.774
Our conversation isn't over yet.

547
36:19.490 --> 36:20.866
Donghyuk.

548
36:35.923 --> 36:38.342
-Do we let him go? -Leave him be.

549
36:38.426 --> 36:43.973
Our goal is to clear Miyuki's name.

550
36:46.058 --> 36:47.893
We have all the evidence now.

551
36:53.524 --> 36:58.154
What you said just now, we will have you repeat it to the police.

552
36:58.237 --> 37:01.365
We have the video, so there's no use keeping quiet.

553
37:01.449 --> 37:05.745
What you did can get you charged with abandonment of a corpse.

554
37:05.828 --> 37:08.873
Mr. Matoba is waiting at the police station.

555
37:08.956 --> 37:11.334
He said, "Let's put an end to the past."

556
37:11.417 --> 37:12.793
It's game over.

557
37:21.302 --> 37:24.972
The murder case of Secretary Nitou, which happened ten years ago,

558
37:25.056 --> 37:26.432
has new developments.

559
37:27.224 --> 37:31.520
Former lawyer Miyuki Shiramoto, currently serving a sentence,

560
37:31.604 --> 37:33.814
is having her retrial request processed,

561
37:33.898 --> 37:37.693
as there is a possibility she was falsely accused.

562
37:39.695 --> 37:41.364
Furthermore, internal documents

563
37:41.447 --> 37:43.991
have surfaced suggesting that after the incident,

564
37:44.075 --> 37:45.868
Furuse's team abused information

565
37:45.951 --> 37:49.705
and lobbied the media in an attempt to direct public opinion.

566
37:50.206 --> 37:53.876
There are increasing demands for the truth to be revealed.

567
37:53.959 --> 37:54.877
Mr. Furuse!

568
37:54.960 --> 37:58.381
They are suspecting you manipulated public opinion ten years ago.

569
37:58.464 --> 38:00.966
This is an extremely regrettable situation.

570
38:01.050 --> 38:04.553
T&amp;U Agency's payment system has been frozen, and there are concerns

571
38:04.637 --> 38:06.597
this might affect the resort project.

572
38:06.680 --> 38:08.140
May I say a few words?

573
38:08.933 --> 38:12.853
For every large project, like this one,

574
38:12.937 --> 38:16.482
people always bring up past failures.

575
38:16.565 --> 38:17.900
Donghyuk.

576
38:18.901 --> 38:20.152
Politics, you see…

577
38:21.278 --> 38:22.905
It's a war.

578
38:23.823 --> 38:25.950
Sacrifices are an inevitable part of it.

579
38:29.703 --> 38:31.122
Please understand that.

580
38:35.126 --> 38:39.839
This resort project is also your father's long-cherished wish.

581
38:41.674 --> 38:43.008
That is precisely why,

582
38:44.677 --> 38:48.931
no matter what happens, I will not give up.

583
38:58.774 --> 39:01.569
Mr. Furuse completely denied the allegations

584
39:01.652 --> 39:04.572
of public opinion manipulation over his secretary's murder.

585
39:04.655 --> 39:09.034
He also emphasized the necessity of the resort project to the public,

586
39:09.118 --> 39:11.078
and left the party headquarters…

587
39:17.751 --> 39:19.336
Ms. Shiramoto,

588
39:20.171 --> 39:22.756
your request for a retrial has been completed.

589
39:23.507 --> 39:27.761
The legal revision has passed too, and I hope we get the results soon.

590
39:29.430 --> 39:30.639
Thank you.

591
39:31.891 --> 39:35.603
We already know you're innocent. Why can't they just let you out?

592
39:35.686 --> 39:36.729
No.

593
39:37.438 --> 39:39.773
It was my fault for not fighting back.

594
39:40.649 --> 39:44.361
Besides, I think a verdict that has been finalized

595
39:45.112 --> 39:47.364
shouldn't be easily overturned.

596
39:48.407 --> 39:53.078
That's why laws are drawn up, and why we lawyers exist.

597
39:57.708 --> 39:58.834
Yukari.

598
40:00.461 --> 40:01.879
Once again,

599
40:04.089 --> 40:05.799
thank you so much.

600
40:08.844 --> 40:10.054
Ms. Shiramoto…

601
40:12.681 --> 40:14.266
You fought for me,

602
40:15.643 --> 40:17.853
risking your own life.

603
40:20.814 --> 40:22.650
I can't thank you enough.

604
40:24.735 --> 40:26.320
It's thanks to you.

605
40:27.821 --> 40:31.408
Your principles made me who I am today.

606
40:36.288 --> 40:38.249
Are you really going to quit?

607
40:40.960 --> 40:44.797
I was never fit to be a lawyer anyway.

608
40:44.880 --> 40:47.007
I agree with you on that,

609
40:47.675 --> 40:50.386
but from here on in will be the hardest part.

610
40:51.637 --> 40:54.723
A retrial request takes a dizzyingly long time to be granted.

611
40:54.807 --> 40:58.811
I think we already have a better person for the job.

612
41:00.479 --> 41:03.607
-I couldn't say this all this time, but… -Yeah?

613
41:16.912 --> 41:20.291
I apologize for the trouble I caused you.

614
41:21.417 --> 41:23.210
What's this?

615
41:23.294 --> 41:25.421
Is it going to snow or something?

616
41:31.260 --> 41:35.848
Once Miyuki is free, the three of us…

617
41:37.016 --> 41:37.975
No,

618
41:40.894 --> 41:42.855
the four of us should go for a drink.

619
41:44.273 --> 41:46.358
I think hell just froze over.

620
41:48.694 --> 41:52.156
Who knew the handwritten note in the article was significant?

621
41:52.239 --> 41:54.575
We have this proof in writing,

622
41:54.658 --> 41:57.786
so even if the testimony changes, this part can be evidence.

623
41:57.870 --> 41:59.997
Mr. Uramawashi saw that far ahead?

624
42:00.080 --> 42:01.707
It sends chills down my spine.

625
42:01.790 --> 42:04.251
Nothing got past him!

626
42:04.335 --> 42:06.045
Online opinion has changed too.

627
42:06.128 --> 42:09.673
That's because the major media are reporting it on a large scale.

628
42:09.757 --> 42:12.843
Now even the public is all "She was innocent!"

629
42:12.926 --> 42:17.431
Public opinion is always so fickle.

630
42:17.514 --> 42:18.849
I'm going home.

631
42:18.932 --> 42:20.184
Goodbye.

632
42:20.267 --> 42:22.227
-Bye. -Bye.

633
42:25.606 --> 42:27.024
Excuse me.

634
42:27.107 --> 42:29.193
Will she stop coming here now?

635
42:29.276 --> 42:30.361
Won't you be sad?

636
42:30.444 --> 42:31.654
Hey, I don't really--

637
42:31.737 --> 42:33.656
Now's the time to tell her how you feel.

638
42:33.739 --> 42:35.366
Do you think I have a chance?

639
42:35.449 --> 42:37.242
-Yeah. -No way in hell.

640
42:37.785 --> 42:39.870
-It's fine… -Do it now!

641
43:28.919 --> 43:31.046
Are you really quitting?

642
43:33.048 --> 43:36.760
Ms. Shiramoto's innocence hasn't been recognized yet, you know.

643
43:37.678 --> 43:39.847
I feel kind of tired.

644
43:39.930 --> 43:40.931
What?

645
43:41.014 --> 43:42.558
I'll leave the rest to you.

646
43:42.641 --> 43:44.143
"Leave it to me," you say…

647
43:44.768 --> 43:47.521
Don't push the most exhausting part onto me!

648
43:47.604 --> 43:50.357
I thought you hated being dragged around by me?

649
43:53.026 --> 43:57.072
From now on, you can fight fair and square,

650
43:57.156 --> 43:59.783
your own way.

651
44:00.868 --> 44:03.120
Do you think you get to say that?

652
44:05.289 --> 44:09.251
Because of you, my convictions are in shreds.

653
44:10.085 --> 44:11.462
It's fine.

654
44:12.129 --> 44:17.092
A foolishly honest person like you can't become like me.

655
44:17.176 --> 44:19.553
Are you complimenting me, or insulting me?

656
44:19.636 --> 44:20.888
I'm complimenting you.

657
44:20.971 --> 44:22.306
That's a lie, isn't it?

658
44:26.310 --> 44:28.187
Thank you for everything.

659
44:30.522 --> 44:31.690
I'm grateful.

660
44:32.357 --> 44:33.776
I bet that's also a lie.

661
44:42.743 --> 44:44.161
Well then…

662
44:49.792 --> 44:51.126
Goodbye.

663
45:03.680 --> 45:05.349
I'm sure that was…

664
45:06.850 --> 45:08.477
also a lie, right?

665
45:26.703 --> 45:27.538
Mr. Fujiwara!

666
45:27.621 --> 45:29.540
My wife and I rarely agreed…

667
45:30.374 --> 45:32.167
I got scammed at a beauty salon.

668
45:32.251 --> 45:34.169
You get a good deal if you start today!

669
45:35.170 --> 45:37.589
There must be an opening somewhere!

670
45:37.673 --> 45:39.800
-You said it was the last time! -Make me your apprentice!

671
45:39.883 --> 45:41.635
You're not fit to be a lawyer.

672
45:42.135 --> 45:44.888
You've become a better lawyer than before.

673
45:44.972 --> 45:45.973
That was a lie.

674
45:46.056 --> 45:47.266
What?!

675
45:47.891 --> 45:48.850
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
